      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "types/property-key-access",
      "title": "`$obj->$key` accepts a `property<T>` and nothing else; a read is the union and a write is checked",
      "status": "shipped",
      "because": ["0126", "0036", "0014", "0038"],
      "divergesFromPhp": "a computed property name is not a string at the site — every other operand is refused, dispatch through a computed *method* name stays refused, and a `readonly` field in the set is refused at the write",
      "seeAlso": ["types/property-key", "types/erased-member-access", "types/property-key-variance"],
      "guardedBy": [
        "tests/conformance/class/a-property-key-reads-and-writes-the-field-it-names.nvst",
        "tests/conformance/lang/a-computed-member-name-is-a-diagnostic.nvst"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "types/unions-and-mixed",
      "title": "A union permits only what every member permits, and `mixed` is the one position checked nowhere",
      "status": "shipped",
      "because": ["0007", "0012", "0066", "0047", "0150"],
      "divergesFromPhp": "there is no `is_int()`-style free function to narrow with — the question is the `is` operator (`rule:types/type-test`) — and `mixed` never absorbs implicitly: `int $n = $m;` is a diagnostic rather than a runtime check",
      "seeAlso": ["types/narrowing", "types/conversion", "types/grammar", "types/mixed-subscript", "types/type-test"],
      "guardedBy": [
        "tests/conformance/lang/a-mixed-value-converts-to-a-scalar-on-request.nvst",
        "tests/conformance/lang/a-mixed-value-answers-arithmetic-truth-and-a-subscript.nvst",
        "tests/conformance/lang/a-union-operand-renders-by-its-runtime-tag.nvst",
        "crates/nvs-types/tests/narrowing.rs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "types/type-test",
      "title": "`$x is T` tests whether a value holds a `T`, answers `bool`, and never refuses because the answer is knowable",
      "status": "shipped",
      "because": ["0150", "0192"],
      "divergesFromPhp": "`int` and `uint` are separate tags, so a `BIGINT UNSIGNED` value answers `is uint` and not `is int` where `is_int()` was true for both, and `string` and `bytes` are separate the same way; `is 3.14` is refused outright, there being no float literal type",
      "seeAlso": ["types/narrowing", "types/conversion", "types/unions-and-mixed", "types/literal-types", "types/class-reference-sites", "php-migration/one-type-test"],
      "guardedBy": [
